ate level material  which is these graded readers and there  again you can search for graded readers  in Spanish I know Ollie Richards in the  UK puts out a good series of graded  readers in these different languages so  you gotta have a strategy that takes you  from the the starter book and that's  almost like it's a given it's that  ladder that gets you up to the next  level but there once you're past that  you have to have a strategy to find that  compelling content content that's  interesting that's accessible to you  that consists of audio and transcript so  that you can then mine the text for  words and phrases so I just wanted to  comment a bit on this whole issue of  listening and people often ask how do  you listen to stuff that you don't  understand of course you don't listen to  stuff that you don't understand you  progress from beginner material as  quickly as possible into compelling  material so that you're actually  motivated to listen to it and read about  things that are of interest to you so  hopefully that is of interest and thank  you for listening and I look forward to  hearing your questions about listening  and finding content and by the way don't  say don't ask me where do I find content  without telling me what language it is  that you're interested in finding  content for but do try to if you don't  know how to say podcast or audio book or  ebook and on history or music or  whatever use Google Translate come up  with a search term and then see what you  can find okay then thanks for listening  and bye for now  [Music]
 

